    {
      "role": "tool",
      "name": "skill_view",
      "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"image-generation-umbrella\", \"description\": \"Class-level umbrella for all image generation — image_generate tool (API), local-gen-queue server (subprocess-based, sequential, SDXL Lightning default), and local diffusers (FLUX, SD35) for batches/img2img. No ComfyUI.\", \"tags\": [\"image-generation\", \"umbrella\"], \"related_skills\": [], \"content\": \"---\\nname: image-generation-umbrella\\ndescription: \\\"Class-level umbrella for all image generation — image_generate tool (API), local-gen-queue server (subprocess-based, sequential, SDXL Lightning default), and local diffusers (FLUX, SD35) for batches/img2img. No ComfyUI.\\\"\\ntags: [image-generation, umbrella]\\ntriggers:\\n  - generating images via API or locally\\n  - FLUX, Stable Diffusion, or SDXL workflows\\n  - img2img style transfer\\n  - batch image generation\\n  - local image generation on Windows with limited VRAM\\n  - Stable Horde worker setup or management\\n  - gallery of generated images\\n---\\n\\n# Image Generation — Class-Level Umbrella\\n\\n## Queue-System\\n\\n**Alle lokalen Generationen laufen über den Queue-Server (Port 8283):**\\n- Sequentiell = 1 Bild = 1 Job = kein VRAM-Crash\\n- Subprocess-basiert = Queue läuft immer, auch wenn Torch fliegt\\n- Watchdog-Cron (alle 2 Min) startet Queue bei Absturz neu\\n- Space-übergreifend: Jeder Space sendet an dieselbe Queue\\n- **Zwei Backends:** Lokales SDXL (GPU-lastig) ODER Stable Horde API (GPU-frei)\\n\\n**API:** `POST http://127.0.0.1:8283/generate`\\n\\n**ComfyUI wird NICHT verwendet.** Alle lokalen Generationen laufen via **diffusers** (SDXL/FLUX) über die Queue.\\n\\n## Backend-Umschaltung (NEU)\\n\\nGen Queue (8283) unterstützt zwei Betriebsmodi:\\n\\n| Backend | GPU-Last | Kudos-Kosten | Latenz | Setup |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `local` | ~6-7 GB VRAM | Keine | ~3-4s (Lightning) | Standard (default) |\\n| `horde` ✅ **Empfohlen** | ~800 MB VRAM | ~11 Kudos/Bild | ~13-30s | `GEN_QUEUE_BACKEND=horde` |\\n\\n**Umschalten:**\\n```bash\\nexport GEN_QUEUE_BACKEND=horde\\nexport GEN_QUEUE_WORKER=/c/HermesPortable/home/scripts/horde_worker.py\\nbash /c/HermesPortable/home/scripts/start_gen_queue.sh\\n```\\n\\n**Horde Worker (Low-VRAM) läuft parallel:**\\n- SD 1.5 (627×627, max_power=12) statt SDXL → ~2-3 GB VRAM\\n- Entlädt Modelle zwischen Jobs (`unload_models_from_vram_often: true`)\\n- Sammelt weiter Kudos während die Queue remote generiert\\n\\n**VRAM-Bilanz (RTX 3060 12GB):**\\n```\\nVORHER:  SDXL lokal (6GB) + Dolphin 8B (6GB) = CRASH\\nNACHHER: Dolphin 8B + Horde Worker + Qwen 9B = 1.575 MB FÜR ALLES\\n```\\n\\n## Sub-Skills & Services\\n\\n| Domain | Skill / Service | When to use |\\n|--------|----------------|-------------|\\n| **API generation** | `image_generate` tool | Quick single images, no local setup |\\n| **Local queue server** | Queue (Port 8283) | **Empfohlen für alle lokalen Generationen** |\\n| **Local FLUX/SDXL batches** | `local-flux-merged-diffusers` | Wenn Queue nicht verfügbar oder Batch-Script |\\n| **Magazin watercolor** | `tirol-magazin-watercolor` | tiroltourismus.com Magazin-Heldenbilder |\\n| **Hardware/Modelle (DE)** | `lokale-bildgenerierung` | Deutsche Übersicht, GPU-Infos, Style-Prefs |\\n| **Provider Pool** | `provider-pool` | Alle API-Provider inkl. Horde-Recipes |\\n| **Horde Details** | `provider-pool references/` | Horde-Keys, Worker Config, Direct API |\\n\\n## Quick Decision (aktualisiert)\\n\\n```\\nBild generieren?\\n├── User hat eigenes System? → Nur Prompt-Templates liefern, KEINE Generation\\n├── GPU soll frei bleiben? → GEN_QUEUE_BACKEND=horde starten, Kudos verbrauchen\\n├── Queue läuft (Port 8283)? → POST /generate → warten\\n├── Queue starten & nutzen? → bash start_gen_queue.sh → POST generate\\n├── Lokale GPU idle + will Kudos sammeln? → start_horde_worker.py start (Low-VRAM)\\n├── image_generate Tool → Schnelle Einzelbilder via API\\n├── lokaler Batch/img2img? → diffusers (local-flux-merged-diffusers Skill)\\n└── Nichts davon? → Nur Prompt-Templates\\n```\\n\\n## Stable Horde (distributed GPU network)\\n\\nWorker unter `C:/HermesPortable/home/horde-worker-reGen/`.\\n\\n**Account:** `PupCid#493646` | **Worker:** `NovaBewusstsein-RTX3060` | **API Key:** `njolKkbw88RDSESdriVoqg`\\n\\n**Live-Status:** 🟢 Online — ~27k Kudos, Low-VRAM Mode (max_power=12, SD 1.5)\\n**Aktuelle Architektur:** Gen Queue forwardet direkt an Horde API (kein lokales SDXL).\\n**Worker läuft separat:** Sammelt Kudos mit Low-VRAM Config, Gen Queue konsumiert Kudos via API.\\n\\n**Philosophie — Fair Play:** GPU teilen wenn idle → Kudos verdienen → Flux/SD3/andere abrufen.\\n\\n**Siehe `provider-pool` Skill für:** Vollständige Key-Liste, Horde API Recipes, Workflow-Details.\\n\\n## Local Gen Queue (Port 8283)\\n\\nDer Queue-Server unter `C:/HermesPortable/home/scripts/local_gen_queue.py` ist der **bevorzugte Weg** für lokale Generationen. Jeder Job läuft als isolierter Subprozess.\\n\\n**Verfügbare Modelle:**\\n\\n| Modell | Steps | Speed | Beschreibung |\\n|--------|-------|-------|-------------|\\n| `sdxl-lightning` 🏆 **Default** | 4 | ~3-4s | 1024×1024, cfg=2.0, scheduler=ddim |\\n| `sdxl-base` | 25 | ~17s | Fallback wenn Lightning-Stil nicht passt |\\n| `sdxl-realvis` | 25 | ~17s | Nur für Photorealismus |\\n\\n**API:**\\n```bash\\n# Job einreihen\\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8283/generate \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"model\\\":\\\"sdxl-lightning\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"ein niedlicher Fuchs\\\",\\\"steps\\\":4}'\\n\\n# Status\\ncurl http://localhost:8283/status/gen_abc123\\n\\n# Queue\\ncurl http://localhost:8283/queue\\n```\\n\\n## Style-Exploration Workflow\\n\\n1. **Pick ONE representative subject** from the content.\\n2. **Generate 5 distinct art styles** of that same subject.\\n3. **Present images inline** via `MEDIA:` paths — no vision_analyze, no HTML previews, no descriptions.\\n4. **Let user pick one style**, then batch-generate all content.\\n\\n**Per-Project Style Preferences:**\\n\\n| Projekt | Bevorzugte Stile | Dokumentiert in |\\n|---------|-----------------|-----------------|\\n| finanz-junkie.de | Scribble/Sketch/Comic/Furry — handgezeichnet, kein Photorealismus | `finanz-junkie-blog-system` → `references/article-image-prompts.md` |\\n| tiroltourismus.com | Watercolor painting | `tirol-magazin-watercolor` |\\n| hostazar.com | Dark cyber/tech aesthetic | Hostazar article templates |\\n| Alle Content-Projekte | Kein Photorealismus | `lokale-bildgenerierung` → User-Style-Preference |\\n\\n## Identity/Persona Exploration\\n\\nGenerate 3-5 conceptual interpretations with distinct archetypes: Ethereal Portrait, Abstract Symbol, Mythic/Archetypal, Digital/AI-native, Elemental/Primordial.\\n\\n## User Presentation Preferences\\n\\n- Show images via `MEDIA:/absolute/path/file.png` in chat.\\n- Do NOT use `vision_analyze` to describe images unless asked.\\n\\n## References\\n\\n| File | Content |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `references/blog-article-image-audit.md` | Batch article image audit + Pillow placeholder fallback workflow |\\n| `references/local-gen-queue.md` | Queue server API docs, architecture, startup |\\n| `references/hermes-venv-sdxl-diffusers.md` | SDXL diffusers recipe via Hermes venv |\\n| `references/identity-persona-prompts.md` | SDXL prompt patterns for AI avatar |\\n| `references/model-selection-and-links.md` | Current model choices and download links |\\n| `references/sdxl-in-cron-workflow.md` | SDXL inline in no_agent cron |\\n| `references/stable-horde-worker.md` | Legacy Horde Worker Setup (Smart Bridge) |\\n| `references/stable-horde-user-api.md` | Horde API als Consumer: Flux/SD3 generieren, Kudos einlösen |\\n| `templates/horde-startup.vbs` | VBS-Script für unsichtbaren Autostart (legacy) |\\n| `references/sdxl-colored-pencil-sketch-heroes.md` | SDXL colored pencil sketch workflow |\\n| `references/sd15-lineart-blog-heroes.md` | SD1.5 lineart furry workflow |\\n| `references/design-pipeline-logo-favicon.md` | Logo + favicon + CSS theme generation |\\n| `references/hybrid-branded-batch-composition.md` | Hybrid branded batch composition |\\n| `references/stable-horde-gallery-upgrade-2026-06.md` | Gallery-Struktur: Today/This Week/User/Older, 14-day cleanup |\\n\\n> **Horde Details (aktualisiert) siehe:** `skill_view(name='provider-pool', file_path='references/horde-integration.md')` — API-Keys, Worker Low-VRAM Config, Direct Python Usage.\\n> `skill_view(name='provider-pool', file_path='references/image-gen-ecosystem.md')` — VRAM-Management, Backend-Switch.\\n\\n## Pitfalls (aktualisiert)\\n\\n1. **🧟 GPU zombie processes** — Failed generations leave Python processes holding VRAM. `gpu-orphan-cleanup` Cron killt sie alle 5 Min. Manuell: `nvidia-smi | grep python` → `taskkill.exe //F //PID <pid>`.\\n\\n2. **🚨 Queue-Server meldet \\\"failed\\\" obwohl Bild OK** — Subprocess exit 1 bug: `finally` block überschreibt `sys.exit(0)` mit exit 1 weil `SystemExit` nicht von `except Exception` gefangen wird. Workaround: `except SystemExit: pass` im Worker. Siehe `horde_worker.py` für fix.\\n\\n3. **🚨 WDDM torch Ausfall nach GPU-Kill** — `torch.cuda.is_available()` → `False`. Fix: `pip install --force-reinstall torch==2.9.1+cu126 torchvision==0.24.1+cu126 --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126`.\\n\\n4. **S3 URLs expire** (~60 min) — download immediately after generation.\\n\\n5. **CLIP token limit is 77 tokens** — keep prompts short.\\n\\n6. **`from_single_file` without config** — Use WITHOUT `config=` to avoid tokenizer errors.\\n\\n7. **SSL cert path** — Set `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` before from_single_file in git-bash.\\n\\n8. **FLUX can't produce transparent PNGs** — use PIL background removal.\\n\\n9. **API 429 rate limiting** — catch HTTPError, sleep 5-10s, retry once.\\n\\n10. **🧟 Queue blocked by cron backlog** — Other cron jobs can fill the queue with 150+ pending jobs. Check `curl http://127.0.0.1:8283/queue` before queueing. Fall back to Pillow placeholder (see `references/blog-article-image-audit.md`).\\n\\n11. **🧟 Horde Worker ignoriert ENV-Vars** — `HORDE_MAX_POWER` etc. werden IGNORIERT. Config MUSS in `bridgeData.yaml` stehen. Nur YAML zählt für den Worker.\\n\\n12. **Horde Worker `pip install -e .` timed out** — Build deps (setuptools) zu schwer. Workaround: `cp -r horde_worker_regen venv/Lib/site-packages/`\\n\\n13. **Gen Queue 101+ Pending Jobs** — Wenn Worker tot ist/zu langsam, killt einfach die Queue (`kill -9 PID`) und startet neu. Pending Jobs sind flüchtig.\\n\", \"path\": \"image-generation\\\\image-generation-umbrella\\\\SKILL.md\", \"skill_dir\": \"C:\\\\HermesPortable\\\\home\\\\skills\\\\image-generation\\\\image-generation-umbrella\", \"linked_files\": {\"references\": [\"references\\\\blog-article-image-audit.md\", \"references\\\\design-pipeline-logo-favicon.md\", \"references\\\\hermes-venv-sdxl-diffusers.md\", \"references\\\\hybrid-branded-batch-composition.md\", \"references\\\\identity-persona-prompts.md\", \"references\\\\local-gen-queue.md\", \"references\\\\sd15-lineart-blog-heroes.md\", \"references\\\\sdxl-colored-pencil-sketch-heroes.md\", \"references\\\\sdxl-in-cron-workflow.md\", \"references\\\\stable-horde-user-api.md\", \"references\\\\stable-horde-worker.md\"], \"scripts\": [\"scripts\\\\horde-batch-generate.sh\"]}, \"usage_hint\": \"To view linked files, call skill_view(name, file_path) where file_path is e.g. 'references/api.md' or 'assets/config.yaml'\", \"required_environment_variables\": [], \"required_commands\": [], \"missing_required_environment_variables\": [], \"missing_credential_files\": [], \"missing_required_commands\": [], \"setup_needed\": false, \"setup_skipped\": false, \"readiness_status\": \"available\"}",
