      "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
      "reasoning_content": "Now I can see it clearly! The silhouette is an oval/capsule shape:\n- Starts at y=176 (12% from top), ends at y=512 (66% from top)\n- Widest part at y=320-368 (30-50% from top)\n- Perfectly symmetric left-right and top-bottom\n- The shape is an ellipse/capsule centered in the image\n\nThis is definitely a programmatically created image! It's a simple capsule/ellipse cutout on a gradient background. The shape is the same for golden retriever AND meerschweinchen - it's just a generic white capsule/oval in the center.\n\nSo the design language is:\n1. **1024×768 canvas**\n2. **Vertical gradient** from lighter color (top) to darker (bottom)\n3. **White capsule/oval** cutout in the center (generic, not actual animal silhouette)\n4. **256-color palette** optimized (indexed PNG style)\n5. **Each species gets its own color theme**\n\nThis is a simple, clean, minimal design that can be easily reproduced programmatically!\n\nFor reptiles, I'll use a warm terracotta/desert sand gradient since that fits the reptile theme.\n\nLet me create a Python script to generate the image.",
