ry regenerating with the sdxl-base model (25 steps) for proper quality. Or use horde.\n\nActually, the queue might have the issue that sdxl-lightning at 4 steps produces very small low-quality images. Let me try with the base model or at least more steps.Die sind nur 5-19KB – viel zu klein für 768×576 (Vergleich: katzenkrankheiten hat 68KB). SDXL Lightning 4 Steps ist zu grob. Ich generiere mit dem Base-Model und 25 Steps für richtige Qualität nach:17 new jobs queued with sdxl-base model (25 steps). The queue already had the 17 Lightning jobs that mostly finished but were too small. Now we have 17 new jobs. Let me wait for the queue to drain, then save them.\n\nBut wait - the previous Lightning jobs are already done (5-19KB each). The Lightning 4-step versions are too small. The new Base 25-step versions should be much better quality and larger file sizes.\n\nLet me wait for the queue...The script timed out but the queue might still be running. Let me check the current status.19 pending with 25 completed - still lots in the queue. The sdxl-base model uses 25 steps instead of 4, so each image takes ~17s instead of ~3-4s. Let me wait longer.Still 12 pending. Let me keep polling at shorter intervals.The script keeps timing out at 300s. The sdxl-base model takes about 17s per image. So 17 images would take about 4.8 minutes. But the queue also has other pending jobs from before (13 old ones + 17 new ones = 30 total). 30 images × 17s = 8.5 minutes. That's over 300s. Let me just check the queue directly.Almost done - only 3 pending but they're old comic-style jobs that were queued earlier, not my new ones. Let me check which of my base-model jobs completed.  response44 completed total. Let me check which of my 17 base-model jobs completed. I need to find the files and save them. 17 saved at 768x576, but only 13-32KB. The reference image (katzenkrankheiten) is 68KB at 768x576. These are still too small. The sdxl-base with 25 steps is giving us low-quality images. \n\nI thi