      "name": "session_search",
      "snippet": "{\"success\": true, \"query\": \"pop art comic haustierzentrum prompt furry\", \"results\": [{\"session_id\": \"4b77609619d4\", \"when\": \"June 04, 2026 at 12:18 AM\", \"source\": \"webui\", \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\", \"summary\": \"## Conversation Summary: GPU Queue Infrastructure & Watchdog Setup\\n\\n### Search Topic Context\\nThe session revolved around resolving VRAM crashes during image generation (including possible pop art comic furry prompts for haustierzentrum.com). Earlier conversation (truncated) involved generation attempts that crashed due to VRAM exhaustion.\\n\\n### What Was Accomplished\\n\\n**Problem Identified:** NVIDIA WDDM driver enters a failed state after killing GPU zombie processes — `import torch` hangs even with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''`. Known Windows issue requiring driver reset.\\n\\n**Queue Server Built** → `C:\\\\HermesPortable\\\\home\\\\scripts\\\\local_gen_queue.py`\\n- REST API on **localhost:8283**\\n- Sequential processing (1 image = 1 job) — **no parallel VRAM crashes**\\n- Each generation runs in a **subprocess** — Torch crashes don't affect the queue\\n- 5-minute timeout per job\\n- Status polling via `GET /status/{id}`\\n\\n**Three Models Configured:**\\n| Model | Steps | Speed |\\n|-------|-------|-------|\\n| **sdxl-lightning** 🏆 default | 4 | ~3-4s |\\n| sdxl-base | 25 | ~17s |\\n| sdxl-realvis | 25 | ~17s |\\n\\n**Auto-Start & Watchdog:**\\n- `start_gen_queue.sh` created → checks port 8283, starts queue if down\\n- **Cron job \\\"gen-queue-watchdog\\\"** runs every 2 minutes → keeps queue alive\\n- `ensure_models.py` patched to include and restart port 8283 alongside LLM models\\n\\n**Skills Patched (all 3):**\\n- `lokale-bildgenerierung` → Queue API reference + code examples\\n- `local-flux-merged-diffusers` → redirects to queue\\n- `image-generation-umbrella` → queue section + updated decision tree\\n\\n**Old Skills Removed:** `comfyui` and `flux-optimization` deleted\\n\\n### GPU Cleanup\\nTwo Python312 diffusers zombies (PIDs 6172, 25848) were killed:\\n- Before: **11,673/12,288 MB** (95%)\\n- After: **1,041/12,288 MB** (8%) — **10.6 GB freed**\\n\\n### Left Unresolved / Notable\\n- Driver was NOT reset this session — user agreed to reboot to clear the WDDM hang\\n- Queue needs PC restart or nvidia driver reset to function initially\\n- Memory entry updated: entry 7 now reads \\\"Bildgen: Queue 8283 (sequentiell, Subprocess). sdxl_lightning ~3-4s. Skills fertig gepatched. WDDM-Pitfall: torch nach GPU-Kill hängend → Reboot.\\\"\\n\\n### Commands & Key Details\\n- Queue server: `python C:\\\\HermesPortable\\\\home\\\\scripts\\\\local_gen_queue.py`\\n- Watchdog script: `C:\\\\HermesPortable\\\\home\\\\scripts\\\\start_gen_queue.sh`\\n- Port: **8283**\\n- After reboot, queue auto-starts within 2 minutes via cron watchdog\"}, {\"session_id\": \"cron_7701ece46b06_20260603_155428\", \"when\": \"June 03, 2026 at 03:54 PM\", \"source\": \"cron\", \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\", \"summary\": \"The user focused on generating and integrating hero images for several blog projects, specifically targeting the \\\"Haustierzentrum\\\" and \\\"Aquaristik Zentrum\\\" repositories.\\n\\n### 1. User Goals\\nThe user wanted to identify articles missing hero images, generate a specific image for a French Bulldog article using a \\\"pop art comic\\\" style, and ensure all articles in the repositories had correctly formatted `<img>` tags and valid file paths.\\n\\n### 2. Actions Taken and Outcomes\\n*   **Audit:** Conducted a file system and content audit across three repositories (`aquarium-zentrum`, `hostazar`, and `haustier-zentrum`).\\n*   **Image Generation:** Used **ComfyUI with SDXL** to generate a hero image for the French Bulldog article.\\n*   **Code Integration:** Inserted `<div class=\\\"article-image-full\\\"><img class=\\\"hero-image\\\"></div>` blocks into 8 articles in the `aquarium-zentrum` repo and 1 article in the `haustier-zentrum` repo.\\n*   **Bug Fixes